Figure 3(a) shows the sensitivity for each indicated ion as a function of the stopping power.14) It is obvious that the stopping power is never the universal parameter of sensitivity for these ions. The restricted energy loss (REL) has been developed and utilized as the best universal param- eter for polymeric etched track detectors, in which higher energy components of secondary electrons are regarded as contribute less to track formation above a certain cut-off energy ω0.1 0.10,15,16) In the case of the poly(ally1 diglycol car- bonate) (PADC) detectors, which is the most sensitive track detector and known under the trade name of CR-39, the appropriate cut-off energy was determined as wo = 200 eV based on the experiments at HIMAC with protons and heavy

