Fourier transform infrared (FTIR) scattered spectra from samples were recorded using the Bruker Vertex 80v FT-IR spectrometer in the reflectance mode (ATR mode). Spectra of the samples were recorded in the range of 600–2500 cm–1 in ambient air at room temperature, with a resolution of 1 cm–1 and accumulation of 32 scans. FTIR was employed to inves- tigate the functional groups present on the PI fi lm surface before and after treatment.

The water static contact angle between the liquid meniscus and the polymer surface was measured by the sessile drop technique. The measurements were performed before and after the plasma treatment of polymer fi lms for 10, 15, and 20 min using an Elektronik & Gerätetechnik Optik SURFTENS contact angle measuring instrument.

Fluorescence spectra were obtained using a Fluorolog 3 spectrofluorometer (Horiba Ivon Jobin), equipped with a 450 W xenon CW lamp, to investigate the optical properties of polyimide films. A double monochromator was used to obtain monochromatic light that passed through polymer films. The light intensity was measured in front of and behind the sample. The light intensity ratio was also calculated.

\begin{title}
3. Results and discussions
